{"surface": "inspector", "title": "Full text", "html": "<header class=\"hero\"><p class=\"kicker\">Full text</p><h2 class=\"title\">benzinga.com</h2><p class=\"ctx\"><a href=\"https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/11/63369577/bitcoin-anthropic-ipo-spacex-selloff-nvidia\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/11/63369577/bitcoin-anthropic-ipo-spacex-selloff-nvidia</a> · read Nov 19, 2026</p></header><div class=\"page md\" data-md=\"# Bitcoin Sank Ahead of SpaceX&#x27;s IPO. Now It&#x27;s Falling Before Anthropic&#x27;s — But for a Different Reason\n\nFive months ago, bitcoin fell ahead of SpaceX’s listing. Whether crypto had to pay the bill for the IPO is less clear.\n\n**Bitcoin** [(CRYPTO: BTC)](https://www.benzinga.com/quote/BTC-USD) fell 19% in the 50 days before SpaceX began trading in June, and it is down 23% over the past 50 days ahead of Anthropic’s debut, according to Block Scholes, an institutional crypto derivatives data firm.\n\nBut the actors have swapped roles.\n\nIn June, AI stocks were booming while crypto bled. This time, AI is leading the selloff.\n\nBitcoin traded near \\$63,940 at 3:30 p.m. ET Tuesday, down 1.4% and about 26% below its Oct. 4 close of \\$86,475.\n\n**Anthropic PBC** is expected to price its IPO on Wednesday, with shares set to begin trading Thursday on the Nasdaq under the ticker ANT. The AI developer has set a range of \\$70 to \\$78 per share.\n\nSo is Anthropic draining money out of crypto? Or is something bigger at work?\n\n## **Two Slides, Almost Identical**\n\nOn the chart, the two declines look like twins. Bitcoin fell 22.4% from its mid-May peak into SpaceX’s debut, and it has dropped 21.3% from its Nov. 4 high ahead of Anthropic’s.\n\n![Bitcoin daily chart, drawdowns ahead of SpaceX and Anthropic IPOs](https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/17142933/bitcoin-spacex-anthropic-tradingview.png)\n\n*Bitcoin daily chart, with the drawdowns ahead of the SpaceX and Anthropic listings. Source: TradingView*\n\nThe backdrop is the opposite.\n\nBefore SpaceX, the Nasdaq-100 rose 11% and **Nvidia Corp.** [(NASDAQ:NVDA)](https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA) gained 3%. This time, Nvidia is down 32% and the Nasdaq-100 is 11% lower over the same window, according to Block Scholes.\n\n“This time, the sell-off has been led by the AI trade itself,” Thahbib Rahman, research analyst at Block Scholes, said in an emailed note Tuesday.\n\n**Read Also: [Dow Slides 1.4% as Salesforce Leads Software Rout Before Anthropic IPO: Stock Market Today](https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/11/63359152/stock-market-today-salesforce-software-selloff-anthropic-ipo-nvidia-november-17)**\n\n## **Bitcoin Now Moves With Nvidia, Not Gold**\n\nBitcoin’s 30-day correlation with Nvidia has climbed from 0.20 at the end of September to 0.56, while its correlation with gold has fallen from 0.63 to 0.39, Block Scholes said.\n\nEarlier this year, bitcoin’s link to gold hit multi-year highs.\n\n“That relationship is weakening and liquidity is ebbing and flowing out of crypto and equities together once more,” Rahman said.\n\nSpot bitcoin ETFs have seen \\$3.0 billion in net outflows in the run-up to the Anthropic listing, according to Block Scholes. The **iShares Bitcoin Trust ETF** [(NASDAQ:IBIT)](https://www.benzinga.com/quote/IBIT) has recorded 11 straight sessions of outflows.\n\n![iShares Bitcoin Trust ETF daily chart with fund flows ahead of the SpaceX and Anthropic listings](https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/17143736/image-360-1024x756.png)\n\n*IBIT ETF daily chart and fund flows, with the drawdowns ahead of the SpaceX and Anthropic listings. Source: TradingView*\n\n## **The Anthropic Theory Has Its Skeptics**\n\n“The Anthropic theory rests on the 20 percent selloff before the SpaceX IPO, but that came at the peak of AI bullishness, the market is through that, and the Anthropic valuation has been falling,” **Jesse Marre**, senior portfolio manager at Hilbert Group, said in emailed comments Monday.\n\nMarre blamed a weekend flush in leveraged positions instead.\n\n“It is much more likely this was simply a stop loss run, and the entire perp market has now basically capitulated,” Marre said.\n\nMarre also cited a hot inflation report that pushed odds of a December Federal Reserve hike to about 90%.\n\nHSBC sees the listing as a possible turning point.\n\n“This week’s Anthropic IPO could well be the next bullish catalyst for tech given likely more reasonable valuations,” Max Kettner, chief multi-asset strategist at HSBC, said in a note Monday.\n\n“We also think it’s very unlikely that even a successful IPO will finally lead to a more ‘trending’ market,” Kettner said.\n\n**Read Also: [Jensen Huang Became AI&#x27;s Insurer of Last Resort: Can Nvidia Now Fulfill a \\$400 Billion Promise?](https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/11/63350356/nvidia-400-billion-commitments-jensen-huang-neoclouds)**\n\n## **What Happened After SpaceX**\n\nBitcoin bottomed 18 days after SpaceX’s listing, closing near \\$58,600 on July 1, and was back above its starting level within 100 days.\n\nHowever, the trigger came from Washington. On Aug. 19, the Treasury announced larger buybacks of longer-dated debt, and bitcoin jumped from about \\$64,700 to \\$78,300 in three sessions.\n\n“That rebound had a clear catalyst of its own, which makes it hard to attribute to capital flowing back from SpaceX,” Rahman said.\n\nThis time, no buyback is on the calendar. Instead, there is an Nvidia earnings report, the year’s second blockbuster IPO and a Fed that markets now expect to hike.\n\n**BTC Price Action:** Bitcoin was down 1.4% at \\$63,940 at the time of publication Tuesday, according to [Benzinga Pro data](https://www.benzinga.com/pro/register-3).\n\n*Photo: Mehaniq / Shutterstock*\" data-base=\"https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/11/63369577/bitcoin-anthropic-ipo-spacex-selloff-nvidia\"></div><p class=\"raw\"><a class=\"rawlink\" data-go=\"raw:src:153\">Full details</a></p>", "wide": true}